From 88cf7ce4237606ca4e7abab845e16519b750a5b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AI <sfslinux@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:06:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(viewer): extend inline Markdown authoring

Add New Page creation plus link and image authoring dialogs.

Render exact underline tags safely, and correct the progress and AT-SPI
lifecycle handling.

Round 2

- Make Alt+P preview path-independent.
- Add an external-editor toolbar button.
- Keep the 11-button formatting toolbar on one row and use an 800x520 default window.
- Make Discard revert the preview.
- Offer Save As in the unsaved-changes dialog.
- Reveal Ctrl+N new pages directly without re-entering the editor toggle path.
- Refresh the i18n POT template for the new user-facing strings.

Round 3

- Give the external-editor button an icon distinct from the inline-editor
  button. A theme without "document-edit" previously fell back onto the
  inline-editor icon, so both toolbar buttons rendered identically.

Round 4

- Keep generated previews in a per-session directory under the temporary
  directory, and drop the directories of instances that are gone. Preview
  files no longer accumulate loose in the temporary directory.
- Add an Export toolbar button that writes the current page as HTML,
  decorated text, plain text, ANSI text or vt100 text, reusing the same
  renderer the command line exposes.
- Share one page-to-renderer resolution between preview and export.

Round 5

- Document using mdview as a command-line converter in --help and in the
  man page, with one example per output format.
